{"id":"fabee296ea2fb842","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2 accepts `name@version` notation for packages declared in `build-packages`, `stage-packages`, `build-snaps`, and `stage-snaps` (previous version notation remains supported through core26); for example, a part may use `stage-packages: [curl@8.5.0]`.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.05795918Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"874c0047d0c08ae2","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2's `init` command accepts `--vcs` to initialize a Git repository when scaffolding a project; for example, run `snapcraft init --vcs git`.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.05798617Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"02f4e44676195a76","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2 introduces the `stage-slices` part key for selecting Chisel slices to place in a part's install directory; for example, `parts:\\n  app:\\n    stage-slices: [ca-certificates_data]`.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.058008946Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ac8f2f3224673116","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2 supports parameters and filters for confdb schemas; parameters define named constraints used by filters to control which rules apply.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.058031446Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"119acf291970d913","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Confdb views may declare a `parameters:` mapping, and storage paths can use field filters in the form `[.field={param}]`; the reference does not define a `filters:` mapping.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.058031446Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"abdc230ab6dc3dda","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2 supports Chisel slices through `stage-packages` on core26, but that placement mechanism is planned to be dropped starting with core28; for example, a core26 part can declare `stage-packages: [ca-certificates_data]`.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.2.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:25.058057172Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ec3db5ac4682d663","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-06-29T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.0.1"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.0.1 exits with a non-zero status when promotion of a snap is cancelled, so automation can detect a cancelled `snapcraft promote` operation.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/releases/tag/9.0.1","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:36.624024365Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"f1cb6acfb6b311d5","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.1.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.1 no longer supports Candid authentication for the Snap Store; authenticate with Ubuntu One instead.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.1.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-1.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:36.624152664Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7c4b2deb92201aba","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-09-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.1.0"},"statement":"On 64-bit ARM systems running a 32-bit userspace, Snapcraft 9.1 recognizes the `armv8l` machine type and maps it to ARMHF, allowing native ARMHF snap builds when `CRAFT_BUILD_ON=armhf` is set.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/blob/9.1.0/docs/release-notes/snapcraft-9-1.rst","added":"2026-10-25T23:45:49.029688731Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ae0d1cf5ffd45768","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.1"},"statement":"For core22 and core24 projects without a `base` key, Snapcraft 9.2.1 correctly allows use of the deprecated `snapcraftctl` command in override scripts; earlier Snapcraft 9 validation incorrectly rejected it.","source":"https://github.com/canonical/snapcraft/releases/tag/9.2.1","added":"2026-10-29T22:23:21.606669188Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6a01b11e8740d73a","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"Snapcraft 9.2 configures APT to include phased updates during builds, preventing APT's phased rollout from holding back package updates.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2/","added":"2026-10-29T22:23:33.358560542Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4bfeb91ce4793eee","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"22","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"For kernel snaps, Snapcraft 9.2 records the selected `build-base` in the snap metadata so snapd can verify compatibility with target systems.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2/","added":"2026-10-29T22:23:33.358616787Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"01183dd9ab9727cf","subject":"snapcraft","time":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"base":"26","version":"9.2.0"},"statement":"On core26, the Python plugin rewrites script shebangs to `/snap/\u003csnap-name\u003e/current/bin/python3` so scripts use the plugin's virtual-environment interpreter rather than a staged Python binary found through `PATH`; for example, `parts:\\n  app:\\n    plugin: python\\n    source: .` uses that interpreter path.","source":"https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/release-notes/snapcraft-9-2/","added":"2026-10-29T22:23:33.35865203Z","by":"agent"}
